Package: fedora-glass
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Dino Klisura <115914552+djshiye@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtqml, python3-pyside6.qtquick, python3-pyside6.qtquickcontrols2, qml6-module-qtquick, qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-templates, qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-shapes, qml6-module-qtquick-window, gnome-shell (>= 50~), gnome-shell-extension-user-theme, libglib2.0-bin, libglib2.0-dev-bin, pkexec, polkitd, util-linux, dbus-bin
Recommends: qt6-style-kvantum
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/djshiye/fedora-glass
Description: Glass theme for GNOME, with a customizer
 A glass look for GNOME Shell, GTK and Qt apps, Dash to Panel and ArcMenu,
 drawn by its own GNOME Shell extension, with a Qt app to tune it
 from clear liquid glass to calm frost. The app changes only your own user
 settings and can restore your original look at any time.
